cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the
  upstream PyUltraLight and PyUltraLight 2 works listed under references.
  If you use the SK features (black holes in solitons, manual dynamical
  friction, the eigenmode decomposition), please also cite the Stone
  Skipping paper (arXiv:2602.11512) listed under references.
type: software
title: "PyUltraLight 2, SK fork (PyUL_SK)"
abstract: >-
  Fork of PyUltraLight 2 used for the black-hole simulations of "Stone
  Skipping Black Holes in Ultralight Dark Matter Solitons": cell-centred
  grids, manual dynamical friction, a resampled centre-of-mass cube and an
  optional inline eigenmode (c_nlm) decomposition, with isolated-potential,
  portability and bug fixes, on top of the upstream split-step
  Schroedinger-Poisson solver with N-body particles.
